    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>The Maratha Empire grew from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/shivaji">Shivaji</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hill-fort">hill forts</a> in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-ghats">Western Ghats</a> into a confederacy that dominated 18th-century <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a>.</li><li>It broke Mughal supremacy, reaching <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/attock">Attock</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indus">Indus</a> in 1758 and later controlling <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/delhi">Delhi</a> and the Mughal emperor.</li><li>Defeat at Panipat in 1761, rivalry among its chiefs and three wars with the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-india-company">East India Company</a> ended its independence in 1818.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>The Marathas built a capable navy with sea forts such as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sindhudurg-fort">Sindhudurg</a>; under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kanhoji-angre">Kanhoji Angre</a> in the early 18th century it challenged even the English and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dutch">Dutch</a>.</p></aside>
    </section>

